<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'"><title>Midnight Express · Local subscriptions</title><meta name="description" content="Explore browser-local subscription controls, bounded delivery and offline reference fixtures with an optional Moth wallet connection."><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="subscriptions.css"><script src="moth-connector.js" defer></script><script src="subscriptions.js" defer></script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a><header><a class="brand" href="index.html"><span class="mark">M∕E</span> MIDNIGHT EXPRESS</a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="index.html#example">Workflows</a><a href="index.html#architecture">Architecture</a><a href="data-model.html">Data model</a><a href="subscriptions.html" aria-current="page">Subscriptions</a><a href="specification.html">Specification</a>
<a href="implementation.html">Implementation</a></nav></header><main id="main-content" tabindex="-1"><section class="demo-intro"><p class="eyebrow">BROWSER LOCAL SIMULATION</p><h1>Your local inbox<span>.</span></h1><p class="lead">Explore local subscriptions and the difference between receiving an event and deciding what to do with it.</p><p>All streams, permissions, cursors and delivery below are a simulation held in this tab's memory. Reload or Reset clears it. Subscribing sends no server request; there is no protocol transport, signing, payment or execution.</p><p>Selectors run locally after authorized decryption in the proposed design. They cannot hide data from an authorized whole-shard reader. This demo has no decryption or production permission service.</p></section><section class="demo-panel" aria-labelledby="wallet-heading"><h2 id="wallet-heading">Optional Moth wallet</h2><p>Moth is an experimental, unaudited reference wallet. Before connecting: Moth grants this origin wallet access, including capabilities beyond this demo's restricted connection-status calls. Connecting is neither network privacy proof nor permission to subscribe. Network: preprod.</p><p id="origin-warning"></p><label class="wallet-consent"><input type="checkbox" id="wallet-ack"> I understand this origin-wide grant can expose balances, addresses and history to other scripts sharing this origin, and persists until revoked in Moth.</label><div class="controls"><button id="discover">Discover Moth</button><button id="connect" disabled>Connect Moth</button><button id="check-wallet">Check wallet status</button><button id="disconnect">Disconnect locally</button></div><p id="wallet-status">Disconnected. Local disconnect cannot revoke the origin grant; manage grants in Moth.</p></section><section class="demo-panel"><h2>Browse streams</h2><div class="form-grid"><label>Search streams<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Quote, payment, renewal…"></label><label>Category<select id="category"><option value="all">All categories</option><option>quotes</option><option>payments</option><option>approvals</option><option>contracts</option><option>credentials</option><option>ops</option></select></label><label>Consumer mode<select id="consumer"><option value="human">Human</option><option value="wallet">Wallet</option><option value="dapp">DApp</option><option value="agent">Agent</option></select></label></div><p id="consumer-help"></p><div id="streams"></div></section><section class="demo-panel"><h2>Subscriptions</h2><p>Demo clock is pinned to 2026-10-04T12:00:00.000Z. Reference fixtures were checked offline by the actual model validator at fixed supplied context; live source and permission are not verified. No browser validator runs. Quotes and approvals are historical on this machine; this dashboard never treats them as actionable.</p><div class="controls"><button id="tick">Simulate intake and delivery</button><button id="process">Mark next item reviewed</button><button id="negative">Simulate rejected quote</button><button id="duplicate">Replay last occurrence</button><button id="gap">Simulate retention gap</button><button id="stale">Expire local permissions</button><button id="revoke">Revoke local permissions</button><button id="reset">Reset demo</button><button id="export">Export mock-only demo state</button></div><p id="permission">Mock local permission: granted.</p><div id="subscriptions"></div></section><section class="demo-panel"><h2>Inbox and quarantine</h2><p>Delivery cursor tracks local receipt; processing cursor tracks contiguous decided dispositions (reviewed or quarantined). Neither proves an action ran or consensus finality. Agent mode prepares no tools or effects. Bounds: two in-flight items, four queued events and 16 KiB per subscription. Backpressure stops scheduling without dropping undecided work.</p><div id="inbox"></div><details><summary>Message detail</summary><pre id="detail">Select an inbox item or stream to inspect the original example and its separate business data.</pre></details></section><p id="announcement" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><noscript>This interactive simulation requires JavaScript. The source fixture examples are static; no production messaging is implemented.</noscript></main></body></html>
